## Why This Is Asked
Tests experience designing scalable, governed data platforms with multi-tenant isolation, data contracts, and end-to-end lineage on GCP. It also probes handling late-arriving data, PII masking, and per-tenant rollback plans.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant isolation in BigQuery with Authorized Views
- Data contracts and lineage via Data Catalog
- Ingestion-time PII masking with DLP
- Event-time processing and late-arrivals in Dataflow
- Cross-region replication and immutable audit logs
- Schema evolution and per-tenant rollback strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: ingest path with DLP masking before storage
const ingest = (record) => {
  const masked = dlp.maskPII(record);
  pubsub.publish(masked);
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test schema evolution across 300 tenants without downtime?
- What metrics and alerting would you implement for cross-region replication health?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to add data quality at streaming scale with per-tenant isolation and governance.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming validation with Great Expectations in Dataflow
- Per-tenant BigQuery partitions and access controls
- DLQ handling, metrics, and rollback tests
- Schema evolution and retention policies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: Dataflow DoFn for validation using GE-like rules
class ValidateFn extends DoFn {
  processElement(ctx){
    const rec=ctx.element;
    if(!valid(rec)){ ctx.output(badTag, rec); } else { ctx.output(goodTag, rec); }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test validating rules with synthetic tenants?
- How would you monitor prod quality drift across tenants and trigger rollbacks?

## Why This Is Asked
Probes multi-tenant data integrity, privacy, and governance at scale, including schema drift handling, masking, and lineage.

## Key Concepts
- Schema registry in Cloud Storage and Drift detection in Dataflow/Beam
- Row-level security with BigQuery policies for per-tenant isolation
- Per-tenant DLP masking and quarantine of invalid data
- Data Catalog lineage and end-to-end observability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-Beam DoFn skeleton for schema validation
class ValidateSchema extends DoFn {
  processElement(context) {
    const record = context.element;
    // load canonical schema from GCS
    // validate fields, types, requireds
    if (valid(record)) {
      context.output(record);
    } else {
      context.output(NOT_VALID, record);
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test schema drift in production without impacting traffic?
- How would you implement rollback across tenants if a schema change breaks downstream queries?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests end-to-end real-time data engineering competencies on GCP, including multi-tenant isolation, dynamic schema evolution, data contracts, and rollback semantics, plus cross-cloud replication and testing strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time ingestion with Pub/Sub and Dataflow templates
- Per-tenant isolation using partitioned BigQuery datasets
- Central schema registry in Data Catalog for dynamic evolution
- End-to-end lineage and data contracts
- 24-hour per-tenant rollback via BigQuery time travel
- Cross-region replication to Snowflake via Snowpipe

## Code Example

```java
// Dataflow pipeline with tenant isolation and schema validation
public class TenantPipeline {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        PipelineOptions options = PipelineOptionsFactory.fromArgs(args).create();
        Pipeline pipeline = Pipeline.create(options);

        pipeline
            .apply("Read from Pub/Sub", PubsubIO.readMessagesWithAttributes()
                .fromSubscription(options.getSubscription()))
            .apply("Extract tenant ID", ParDo.of(new ExtractTenantDoFn()))
            .apply("Validate against schema", ParDo.of(new SchemaValidationDoFn()))
            .apply("Write to tenant BigQuery", new TenantBigQueryWrite());

        pipeline.run();
    }
}
```
